{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785994413444230001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"tarry-creep-range","assignee":"","attestations":{"plan-review":{"algorithm":"HMAC-SHA256","author":"Iso Tester","head_sha":"db3be27b493638b3f2a7d1766709d974489da747","key_id":"412fa5372ad877e0","kind":"plan-review","manifest":["plan-review: PASS","ticket: c38b-98c3-b5cc-410c","material: 7b00e033463e1a91","model: claude-opus-4-8","runner: pydantic_ai","blocking: 0","advisory: 10","regver: 0dbaa5513314ac56","verified-at-sha:db3be27b493638b3f2a7d1766709d974489da747","dep 7f039ecdde81adbf59a786583c05128f74181ea6f60a75d1e9b76c3c52840fb6 src/rebar/llm/prompt_library.py","dep d6ae7366c9951bc56a7d62454b29bcd2a9f39412f8e3c83f3996627d75a81634 src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor.py","dep 5df8b3921024fa78255269e0c4fe99ef82b065b68b044396bbf8fece0e0b8025 src/rebar/llm/workflow/prompt_authoring.py"],"signature":"4e71799ffc841a725828ea8b99621e5eed9855e34ea97bf539ac76619511455a","signed_at":1782677062360297000}},"author":"Iso Tester","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":6},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1782605237804960001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[],"description":"RISK 1 (cross-session duplication) + client reliability. Two competing prompt-authoring WRITE backends both wired into the editor: `prompt_authoring.save_prompt` (atomic temp-file + `os.replace`) and `prompt_library.create_prompt` (NON-atomic `path.write_text`, `prompt_library.py:240`). They write the same `.rebar/prompts/<id>.md` with divergent semantics — one atomic, one a latent half-write on crash; one rejects uppercase ids, the other accepts them.\n\n## Why\n`prompt_library` was added as an \"additive\" layer without folding in the pre-existing atomic writer two directories away. The editor exposes BOTH `/prompt/save` and `/library/create` POST endpoints (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor.py`), so a client can corrupt a prompt file via the non-atomic path. `create_prompt` is essentially a strict subset of `save_prompt` minus the atomicity + id-rule guarantees.\n\n## What / files\n- `src/rebar/llm/prompt_library.py:236-245` — make `create_prompt`/`_write` DELEGATE to `prompt_authoring.save_prompt` (project-forced target) instead of `path.write_text`.\n- Pick ONE id rule (prefer `prompt_authoring._valid_id`); reconcile `PromptExistsError` vs `PromptWriteError` semantics.\n- `src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor.py` — route `/library/create` through the atomic writer.\nKeep the `enumerate_library`/criterion-kind classification that `prompt_library` legitimately adds (only the WRITE path is duplicated, not the enumerate path).\n\n## Scope\nIn: one atomic write path, one id rule, shared error semantics. Out: the enumerate/classification surface (keep), the prompt schema/front-matter format.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] All prompt writes (both editor endpoints) go through the atomic `os.replace` writer — no `write_text` write path remains.\n- [ ] A single id-validation rule governs both endpoints (documented).\n- [ ] A crash/interrupt mid-write cannot leave a partially-written `.rebar/prompts/<id>.md` (test via a write that fails before replace).\n- [ ] Existing prompt-authoring + library tests pass; `enumerate_library` behavior unchanged.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/prompt_library.py","reason":"delegate create_prompt to atomic save_prompt"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/prompt_authoring.py","reason":"canonical atomic writer"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor.py","reason":"route /library/create through atomic writer"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","5ca8-5993-ca83-40f1"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"5ca8-5993-ca83-40f1","parent_status_uuid":"e2c02abf-1f79-4112-9bdd-128ae2669e42","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["audit-2026-06-27","oss-remediation"],"ticket_id":"c38b-98c3-b5cc-410c","ticket_type":"task","title":"Risk 1: consolidate the two prompt-authoring write backends","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["fc7be5ce-177b-4477-9711-c0d45656c8d8","5fa92c20-49e0-43b3-967b-5e7f96e20726","78a1b236-4cad-4af3-94bb-77221d6af60c","5ba043fb-f7e1-4cc8-9e4b-9a11d13db66d","deb93490-d044-4b76-b574-9ab6df53e57d","b4d80601-f5a1-4f1a-9772-347519ff6043","740aa2a5-ea4a-43f2-a0f9-5fbcf111bedf","e2c02abf-1f79-4112-9bdd-128ae2669e42","2a601ecb-2104-4e05-a112-bd467857143a","543e7e11-d7bb-4e1a-a02c-ed33a3d1be53"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785994413444230001,"uuid":"4f359f4f-d028-454d-90b3-1323fc24539e"}